  "notes": [
    "अपना (own) points back to the subject: मैं अपने परिवार के साथ रहता हूँ, \"I live with my (own) family\". मेरे परिवार के साथ is also heard, but अपने is more natural here.",
    "रहता / रहती agrees with the speaker. With आप and तुम, it is रहते for a man and रहती for a woman.",
    "फ़्लैट is masculine, so it is बड़ा and छोटा. Many Indian families live together: grandparents, parents and children in one home."
  ]
